CM ============================================================
CM  doppler_ring_2m.nec — TM-ADF-NEC-003 Rev A
CM  4-Element Doppler Ring Array, 2-meter band
CM  Frequency: 146 MHz
CM  Array: 4 quarter-wave verticals on 0.5λ diameter circle
CM
CM  Element geometry:
CM    Diameter of circle: 1027 mm = 1.027 m (0.5λ at 146 MHz)
CM    Radius: 0.5135 m
CM    Element positions (top view):
CM      E1 (N): (0, +0.5135, 0)
CM      E2 (E): (+0.5135, 0, 0)
CM      E3 (S): (0, -0.5135, 0)
CM      E4 (W): (-0.5135, 0, 0)
CM    Each element: λ/4 = 0.514m above ground plane
CM    Element wire: 5mm aluminum rod (radius=0.0025m)
CM    Ground plane: modeled as 8 radials at z=0
CM
CM  This model: single element active (E1), others parasitic.
CM  To simulate Doppler switching: run 4 separate models with
CM  different active element each time, compare far-field phase.
CM ============================================================
CE
CM
CM --- E1 (North): vertical monopole ---
GW 1 10 0.0 0.5135 0.0 0.0 0.5135 0.514 0.0025
CM --- E2 (East) ---
GW 2 10 0.5135 0.0 0.0 0.5135 0.0 0.514 0.0025
CM --- E3 (South) ---
GW 3 10 0.0 -0.5135 0.0 0.0 -0.5135 0.514 0.0025
CM --- E4 (West) ---
GW 4 10 -0.5135 0.0 0.0 -0.5135 0.0 0.514 0.0025
CM
CM Radial ground plane (8 radials, λ/4 each = 0.514m)
CM Each at z=0, from near origin (0.02m clearance) outward
GW 5  8  0.02 0.0  0.0  0.53  0.0  0.0  0.001
GW 6  8 -0.02 0.0  0.0 -0.53  0.0  0.0  0.001
GW 7  8  0.0  0.02 0.0  0.0   0.53 0.0  0.001
GW 8  8  0.0 -0.02 0.0  0.0  -0.53 0.0  0.001
GW 9  8  0.014 0.014 0.0  0.374  0.374 0.0  0.001
GW 10 8 -0.014 0.014 0.0 -0.374  0.374 0.0  0.001
GW 11 8  0.014 -0.014 0.0  0.374 -0.374 0.0  0.001
GW 12 8 -0.014 -0.014 0.0 -0.374 -0.374 0.0  0.001
CM
CM End geometry, real ground
GE 1
CM
CM Average ground
GN 2 0 0 0 13.0 0.005
CM
CM Frequency: 146 MHz
FR 0 1 0 0 146.0 0
CM
CM Source on E1 (North element) base
EX 0 1 1 0 1.0 0.0
CM
CM Azimuth pattern (elevation=10°, azimuth 0–360°, 5° steps)
RP 0 1 73 1000 10.0 0.0 0.0 5.0
CM
CM Elevation pattern (azimuth=0°, elevation 0–90°, 2° steps)
RP 0 46 1 1000 0.0 0.0 2.0 0.0
CM
EN

CM ============================================================
CM  DOPPLER SIMULATION PROCEDURE:
CM
CM  Run this model 4 times, changing the EX card each time:
CM    Run 1: EX 0 1 1 0 1.0 0.0   (E1=N active)
CM    Run 2: EX 0 2 1 0 1.0 0.0   (E2=E active)
CM    Run 3: EX 0 3 1 0 1.0 0.0   (E3=S active)
CM    Run 4: EX 0 4 1 0 1.0 0.0   (E4=W active)
CM
CM  For a signal from bearing θ:
CM    V_received = E_field × cos(array_angle - θ)
CM    Phase of switching-rate subcarrier = θ (bearing to transmitter)
CM
CM  EXPECTED PATTERN (single active element):
CM    Omnidirectional azimuth (monopole pattern)
CM    Typical gain: 1–2 dBi depending on ground
CM    F/B: N/A (omnidirectional)
CM
CM  BEARING FROM DOPPLER:
CM    When 4 elements switch at 1kHz, the received signal carries a
CM    1kHz AM/PM modulation whose phase = bearing of transmitter.
CM    Phase measured by Goertzel algorithm in ESP32 firmware.
CM ============================================================
